= Timeline of the RSDRP(O) and Russia (until 1926)

*I cannot state just how WIP the lore is, so bear with me as I stumble through this.*

**1898**: The RSDRP is formed as a merger of the League of Struggle for the Emancipation of the Working Class, headed by Lenin, Martov, and others, the General Jewish Labour Bund, representing many of Russia's Jewish Social Democrats, and other Social Democrats who organized around the Rabochaya Gazeta, a Kyivan Social Democratic Newspaper.

**1912**: The RSDRP splits between Lenin's supporters, "<span style="color: #D40000;">**Bolsheviks**</span>", and Martov's supporters, "<span style="color: #ED1B34;">**Mensheviks**</span>."

**1914**: The Great War begins.

**Mar., 1917**: The February Revolution deposes the <span style="color: #FF9C00;">**Tsar**</span> and establishes a Constituent Assembly.

**Aug., 1917**: The <span style="color: #DA291C;">**RSDRP(M)**</span> rebrands to the <span style="color: #ED1B34;">**Russian Social Democratic Labour Party (United)**</span>.

**1918**: The October Revolution begins; In the Party, the <span style="color: #DA291C;">**Internationalist**</span>-wing sides with the <span style="color: #D40000;">**Bolsheviks**</span>, hoping to moderate their followers, while the majority of the <span style="color: #ED1B34;">**RSDRP(O)**</span> sides against them, aligning with the Liberals and Conservatives of the **White Army**.

**Aug., 1918**: Vladimir Lenin is assassinated by Fanny Kaplan, a half-blind <span style="color: #B4121A;">**Narodist**</span>, because of the <span style="color: #D40000;">**Communist**</span> ban on the <span style="color: #990000;">**PLSR**</span> and other <span style="color: #ff0000;">**Leftist**</span> Parties. She is killed by the <span style="color: #D40000;">**Bolsheviks**</span> as a result.

**1920 - North Russia**: British forces, who landed near Murmansk and Arkhangelsk in 1919, advance down Karelia and towards Petrograd. The <span style="color: #D40000;">**Red Army**</span> suffers decisive defeats at the hands of Pavel Bermondt-Avalov's <span style="color: #FF9C00;">**Russkaya Zapadnaya Dobrovol'cheskaya Armiya**</span> and British Expeditionary Forces. 

**1920 - South Russia**: The <span style="color: #0057B7;">**Ukrainian Peo**</span><span style="color: #FFD700;">**ple's Republic**</span>, initially established by Russia, and the <span style="color: #d90012;">**Trans**</span><span style="color: #0098c3;">**cauca**</span><span style="color: #888888;">**sian DFR**</span> push into Southern Russia as the <span style="color: #D40000;">**Red Army**</span> retreats.

**1920 - Siberia**: The combined forces of the Eser-backed <span style="color: #B4121A;">**Narodnaya Armiya KOMUCha**</span>, the <span style="color: #0032A0;">**Československé Legie/Československé Légie**</span>, **Western Expeditionary Forces** and the <span style="color: #888888;">**Sibirskaya**</span> <span style="color: #008000;">**Armiya**</span> deal a harsh blow to local <span style="color: #D40000;">**Bolsheviks**</span> partisans, securing the <span style="color: #888888;">**Far-**</span><span style="color: #008000;">**East**</span> and <span style="color: #888888;">**Sibe**</span><span style="color: #008000;">**ria**</span> for Chernov and Kerensky's Republic. <span style="color: #0057B7;">**Ukr**</span><span style="color: #FFD700;">**ine**</span> remains independent and cautious, though the <span style="color: #d90012;">**Trans**</span><span style="color: #0098c3;">**cauca**</span><span style="color: #888888;">**sian DFR**</span> and <span style="color: #2b6631;">**Central**</span> <span style="color: #87ceeb;">**Asia**</span> re-join Russia as autonomies after long negotiations.

**1921**: Moscow is captured by Lavr Kornilov's **Volunteer Army**, while Petrograd is captured by the British, who turn it over to Kornilov's control. The <span style="color: #D40000;">**Communists**</span> surrender, their leadership is largely imprisoned or executed without trial, and a second Constituent Assembly is organized by Kornilov. The new assembly, dominated by Esers and Kadets, ratifies the Russian Constitution of 1921, and calls for new elections.

**Dec., 1921**: The 1921 Elections finish and <span style="color: #F48100;">**Georgy Lvov**</span>, an independent republican and universally-respected Liberal, is elected President of Russia. In the State Duma, the party-list proportional method results in the <span style="color: #b4121a;">**PSR**</span> emerging as the largest party, followed by the <span style="color: #0087dc;">**Kadets**</span>, then the <span style="color: #ED1B34;">**RSDRP(O)**</span>, and finally the national-conservative <span style="color: #004090;">**VS**</span>. A <span style="color: #ff0000;">**Trudovaya Koalitsiya**</span> is established of the <span style="color: #b4121a;">**PSR**</span>-<span style="color: #ED1B34;">**RSDRP(O)**</span> and other <span style="color: #ff0000;">**Left**</span>-wing parties.

**1922**: The Treaty of Rapallo is signed, which normalized relations with <span style="color: #000000;">**Ger**</span><span style="color: #ff0000;">**ma**</span><span style="color: #ffcc00;">**ny**</span>. Talks with <span style="color: #000000;">**Ger**</span><span style="color: #ff0000;">**ma**</span><span style="color: #ffcc00;">**ny**</span>, largely despised by the population, causes the <span style="color: #ff0000;">**Labor Coalition**</span> to collapse and new elections are held.

**1923**: A "<span style="color: #888888;">**Ru**</span><span style="color: #0032a0;">**ss**</span><span style="color: #DA291C;">**ia**</span> **Coalition**" of the <span style="color: #b4121a;">**PSR**</span>, <span style="color: #0087dc;">**Kadets**</span>, <span style="color: #008000;">**Alash**</span>, and other minor <span style="color: #0087dc;">**Liberal**</span> to <span style="color: #004090;">**Conservative**</span> parties is formed, marking a shift towards Conservative rule. Notably, the Solidarists emerge as a fringe party.

**1924**: <span style="color: #F48100;">**Georgy Lvov**</span> is re-elected President.

**1925**: President <span style="color: #F48100;">**Lvov**</span> dies, and new presidential elections are held, leading to the landslide election of Lavr Kornilov, who ran at the urging of the <span style="color: #004090;">**Conservative**</span> <span style="color: #B4121A;">**Narodist**</span> and Nationalist, Boris Savinkov. Kornilov, a <span style="color: #004090;">**conservative**</span>, war hero, and anti-<span style="color: #D40000;">**Communist**</span>, prevents the <span style="color: #ED1B34;">**RSDRP(O)**</span> from entering government in the 1925 general elections. Biannual elections lead to a continued <span style="color: #888888;">**Ru**</span><span style="color: #0032a0;">**ss**</span><span style="color: #DA291C;">**ia**</span> **Coalition**, though with a meager 52% majority, compared to a previous 63%.

**Jan., 1926**: The incumbent <span style="color: #888888;">**Ru**</span><span style="color: #0032a0;">**ss**</span><span style="color: #DA291C;">**ia**</span> **Coalition** collapses over rural taxation disputes, new elections are scheduled in five months.

