@parties
go-to: menu
set-bg: img/neorevs.jpg
face-image: img/VoteSocDem.jpg

<span style="color: #ED1B34;">**RSDRP(O)**</span> - *Rossijskaja Social-Demokratičeskaja Rabočaja Partija (Ob’jedinjonnaja)* (Russian Social Democratic Labour Party (United)) - this is us. We are a socialist and democratic party of the working class. We are the heirs of the legacy of Marx and Engels, Martov and Plekhanov. We are the foremost defenders of the Republic. The modern RSDRP(o) is the continuation of the Menshevik sections of the RSDRP.

<span style="color: #b4121a;">**PSR**</span> - *Pártiya Sotsialístov-Revolyutsionérov* (Party of Socialists-Revolutionaries) - a left-populist, Narodist party that supports the Republic, and has historically supported many of our labor, welfare, and anti-militarist priorities. They have often been in coalitions with us.

Current relations: [+ psr_relation : relationships +]

<span style="color: #0087dc;">**K-D**</span> - *Konstitutsionno-Demokraticheskaya Partiya/Pártiya Naródnoy Svobódy* (Constitutional Democratic Party, or officially the Party of People's Freedom) - a centrist to center-right liberal party, popular among the intelligensia and educated middle class. They have historically been cordial with us but, especially following their recent conservative turn, oppose our economic policies. The <span style="color: #008000;">**Alash Party**</span> is closely tied to the Kadets, generally considered to be their sister-party in Russian Central Asia. [? if year >= 1930 : They have recently reformed themselves as the German State Party (DStP). ?]

Current relations: [+ musavat_relation : relationships +]

<span style="color: #004090;">**VS**</span> - *Vserossiyskiy Soyuz* (All-Russian Union) - a conservative, nationalist, and often monarchist party, supported by the middle classes and rural conservatives. They despise us.

Current relations: [+ vs_relation : relationships +]

<span style="color: #3bb9ff;">**Müsavat Party**</span> - *Müsavat Firqəsi* (Müsavat Party) - a pan-Muslim liberal party, with pan-Turkist, conservative, and even Socialist elements. It is supported by a broad coalition of Muslims, from left to right. We have entered coalition talks with them before, though they led to nowhere.

Current relations: [+ kadets_relation : relationships +]

<span style="color: #990000;">**PLSRI**</span> - *Partiya Levykh Sotsialistov-Revolyutsionerov-Internatsionalistov* (Party of Left Socialist-Revolutionaries-Internationalists) - a radical left-wing offshoot of the PSR that emerged in the aftermath of the Civil War, they are split between Syndicalists and Revolutionary Narodists.

Current relations: [+ plsri_relation : relationships +]

<span style="color: #D40000;">**RKP(b)**</span> - *Rossiyskaya Kommunisticheskaya Partiya (bol'shevikov)* (Russian Communist Party of Bolsheviks) - The Party of Lenin, despite their failure to overthrow the government at the end of the 1910s and leading into the '20s, the Bolsheviks have legally reorganized thanks to constitutional protections for political groups.

Current relations: [+ rkp_relation : relationships +]

[? if rsrpi_formed: <span style="color: #d84c4c;">**rsrpi**</span> - *Rossiyskaya Sotsialisticheskaya Rabočaja Partiya Internatsionalistov* (Russian Socialist Labor Party of Internationalists) - a party recently formed in a split from the RSDRP(O), the RSRPI is essentially an agglomeration of various left-wing splinter groups between the RSRDP(O) and RKP(B), but is mainly composed of our old Left-wing. ?]

<span style="color: #F9DA00;">**NTS**</span> - *Narodno-trudovoy Soyuz Rossiyskikh Solidaristov* - (National Alliance of Russian Solidarists, or Solidarists) - a far-right ultranationalist, corporatist, and reactionary party. Led by Duke Sergei Nikolaevich Leuchtenberg, many of their members and leaders supported monarchist and nationalist groups in the Civil War.

Current relations: [+ nts_relation : relationships +]

**Other Parties** - there is a multitude of small parties or movements, ranging from conservative to socialist. Parties such as the Labourist Popular-Socialist Party, the Armenian Populist Party, the All-Peasant Union, and others are often grouped together, regardless of ideology. Their political position usually lies between the RSDRP and K-D.

