**Paramilitary groups:**

**Soyuz Fevralya** (SF): The *Union of February* is an organization affiliated with many of the left-democratic parties - the RSDRP, PSR, Left-Kadets and other minor groups, but primarily with the RSDRP due to the organization's urban roots. Historically, this has been an unarmed organization.

Strength: [+ rb_strength +] thousand

Militarization: [+ rb_militancy : militancy +]

**Krasnaya Gvardiya (KG)**: The "*Red Guard*" is associated with the PLSRI and the Bolsheviks.

Strength: [+ rfb_strength +] thousand

Militarization: [+ rfb_militancy : militancy +]

**Russkiy Obshche-Voinskiy Soyuz (ROVS)**: A right-wing, nationalist organization mainly composed of Great War veterans, the *Russian All-Military Union* has no official stance on the Republic, hosting both pro- and anti-republican voices. Associated with the conservative and right-democratic parties, including the Right-Kadets and VS.

Strength: [+ sh_strength +] thousand

Militarization: [+ sh_militancy : militancy +]

**Soyuz Rossiyskoy Narodnoy Molodezhi (SRNM)**: The *Union of Russian National Youth* is the amalgamation of previous Black-Hundredist, Monarchist, and Reactionary paramilitaries into one, they are associated with the Solidarists and stand for Russian autrocracy, dictatorship, and Solidarism.

Strength: [+ sa_strength +] thousand

Militarization: [+ sa_militancy : militancy +]

**Official military/paramilitary groups:**

**Russkaya Armiya**: [+ reichswehr_strength +] thousand troops. This is Russia's military.

Loyalty: [+ reichswehr_loyalty : loyalty +]

**Worker's Militsiya**: [+ prussian_police_strength +] thousand members.

Loyalty: [+ prussian_police_loyalty : loyalty +]



@factions
go-to: neorevisionists if neorevisionism > 0; menu if neorevisionism <= 0
set-bg: img/groupphoto.jpg
face-image: img/disunity.jpg

**Internal factions of the RSDRP**

Overall dissent: [+ dissent_percent : dissent +]

**Internationalists**

The Internationalists are the left-wing of the RSDRP(O), they are Orthodox Marxists who believe that class struggle, historical materialism, and revolutionary socialism are the principles that should guide the Party. They tend to occupy positions between our Center and the Bolsheviks.
Strength: [+ left_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ left_dissent : dissent +]

**Centrists**

The Centrists in the RSDRP(O) are followers of the doctrine of orthodox Marxism as expounded by Karl Kautsky and Julius Martov. They seek a middle course between reform and revolution, while defending the democratic republic.

Strength: [+ center_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ center_dissent : dissent +]

**Labor**

Many RSDRP(O) members are also part of the Vseobshchya Konfederatsya Profsoyuzov (VKP), or General Confederation of Trade Unions. Their goal is economic reform and benefits for organized workers.

Strength: [+ labor_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ labor_dissent : dissent +]

**Liquidationists**

The Liquidationists are pragmatic participants in government, and seek to expand the welfare state and defend democracy against the conservatism, ultranationalism, and revolution. The Liquidationists are the party-right, composed of Great War Defencists and young Socialists alike. [? if rsdrp_prussia : They are dominant in the state governments of West Russia. ?]

Strength: [+ reformist_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ reformist_dissent : dissent +]

@neorevisionists
go-to: menu

**Neodefencists**

Neodefencists focus on defending the republic and expanding democracy, while also expanding the party's base beyond the working class to create a people's party. They support new propaganda methods and extraparliamentary action in defense of the republic.

Strength: [+ neorevisionist_strength : strength +]

Dissent: [+ neorevisionist_dissent : dissent +]


@figures
title: Figures and Charts
set-bg: img/duma.jpg
go-to: menu
on-display: {!
data = [
    {
        "id": "rkp",
        "legend": "RKP",
        "name": "RKP",
        "seats": Q.rkp_r*7.67,
    }];
if (Q.rsrpi_formed && Q.rsrpi_r) {
    data.push({
            "id": "rsrpi",
            "legend": "RSRPI",
            "name": "RSRPI",
            "seats": Math.round(Q.rsrpi_r*7.67),
            });
}
data = data.concat([
    {
        "id": "rsdrp",
        "legend": "RSDRP",
        "name": "RSDRP",
        "seats": Q.rsdrp_r*7.67,
    },
    {
        "id": "plsr",
        "legend": "PLSRI",
        "name": "PLSRI",
        "seats": Q.plsr_r*7.67,
    },
    {
        "id": "musavat",
        "legend": "Müsavat",
        "name": "Müsavat",
        "seats": Q.musavat_r*7.67,
    },
    {
        "id": "psr",
        "legend": "PSR",
        "name": "PSR",
        "seats": Q.psr_r*7.67,
    },
    {
        "id": "kadets",
        "legend": "K-D",
        "name": "K-D",
        "seats": Q.kadets_r*7.67,
    },
    {
        "id": "other",
        "legend": "Other Rightists",
        "name": "Other Rightists",
        "seats": Q.other_r*7.67,
    },
    {
        "id": "otherleft",
        "legend": "Other Leftists",
        "name": "Other Leftists",
        "seats": Q.otherleft_r*7.67,
    },
    {
        "id": "vs",
        "legend": "VS",
        "name": "VS",
        "seats": Q.vs_r*7.67,
    },
    {
        "id": "nts",
        "legend": "NTS",
        "name": "NTS",
        "seats": Q.nts_r*7.67,
    },
]);
if (d3 && window) {
    // get screen width
    var width = 500;
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50;
        height = width;
        document.getElementById("State Duma").style.height = screenWidth/2 + "px";
    }
    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select("#State Duma").datum(data).call(parliament);

    var lines = d3.linegraph(false, false,
            Q.parties,
            {'rsdrp': '#ED1B34', 'rkp': '#D40000', 'plsr': '#990000', 'musavat': '#3bb9ff', 'psr': '#b4121a', 'kadets': '#0087dc', 'vs': '#004090', 'nts': '#F9DA00', 'other': '#a0a0a0', 'otherleft': '#ff0000', 'rsrpi': '#c40000'},
            {'rsdrp': 'RSDRP', 'rkp': 'RKP', 'plsr': 'PLSRI', 'musavat': Q.musavat_name, 'psr': 'PSR', 'kadets': 'K-D', 'vs': 'VS', 'nts': 'NTS', 'other': 'Others', 'otherleft': 'Other Leftists', 'rsrpi': 'RSRPI'});
    lines.width(width).height(400);
    //var svg = lines(Q.election_records);
    if (Q.election_records.length > 0) {
        d3.select("#election_history").datum(Q.election_records).call(lines);
    }
    //document.getElementById('election_history').innerHTML = svg.outerHTML;

    // party support records should not have so many ticks
    if (!Q.historical_mode || Q.game_over) {
        var lines_2 = d3.linegraph(true, true,
            Q.parties,
            {'rsdrp': '#ED1B34', 'rkp': '#D40000', 'plsr': '#990000', 'musavat': '#3bb9ff', 'psr': '#b4121a', 'kadets': '#0087dc', 'vs': '#004090', 'nts': '#F9DA00', 'other': '#a0a0a0', 'otherleft': '#ff0000', 'rsrpi': '#c40000'},
            {'rsdrp': 'RSDRP', 'rkp': 'RKP', 'plsr': 'PLSRI', 'musavat': Q.musavat_name, 'psr': 'PSR', 'kadets': 'K-D', 'vs': 'VS', 'nts': 'NTS', 'other': 'Others', 'otherleft': 'Other Leftists', 'rsrpi': 'RSRPI'});
        lines_2.width(width).height(400);
        d3.select("#party_support_history").datum(Q.party_support_records).call(lines_2);
    }

    // economic stats
    var minInflation = d3.min(Q.economic_records, d => d.inflation);
    var maxUnemployment = d3.max(Q.economic_records, d => d.unemployment);
    var lines_3 = d3.linegraph(true, true, ['inflation', 'unemployment'],
            {'inflation': '#0000FF', 'unemployment': '#FF0000'},
            {'inflation': 'Inflation', 'unemployment': 'Unemployment'},
            maxUnemployment + 5, minInflation - 5, 21);
    lines_3.width(width).height(300);
    d3.select("#economic_history").datum(Q.economic_records).call(lines_3);
}
!}

